# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 93-96 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 11 — CHAPTER 13, 2026-09-21; the one run): the sons of Belial and the inquiry (93), the sword
# and the ban (94), the spoil, the whole offering and the heap (95), the devoted thing, the mercy and the footer (96:1-8 — rows 9-12 are 14:1's, chapter 14's
# sitting) — EVERY ROW READ WHOLE in both files (the whole-row rule); every quotation CUT by consonants (ch13_ink.SP_); a middah named only where the row argues
# by one (logic/MIDDOT.md, the code checked before it is typed). Speed ruling (c): CONTEXT rows terse. Chapter 12's form.
from ch13_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(93, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"MEN HAVE GONE OUT" (13:14) — MEN AND NOT WOMEN; MEN AND NOT MINORS; MEN — NOT FEWER THAN TWO. The head row of piska 93 ({SP_(93, 1, "אנשים", "אין", "פחות", "משנים")} "men — not fewer than two"): THE SEDUCERS\' PARAMETERS from one noun — adult, male, two at least (Tosefta Sanhedrin 14:2). Fresh.')
srow(93, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'"SONS OF BELIAL" — WITHOUT A YOKE: MEN WHO THREW OFF THE YOKE OF THE OMNIPRESENT. ({SP_(93, 2, "בלי", "עול")} "without a yoke"): E30 (checked — the word split into its parts). Fresh.')
srow(93, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"FROM YOUR MIDST" — AND NOT FROM THE BORDER. ({SP_(93, 3, "ולא", "מן", "הספר")} "and not from the border"): a border city is not condemned (Tosefta Sanhedrin 14:1) — the place a condition. Fresh.')
srow(93, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HAVE DRAWN AWAY THE INHABITANTS OF THEIR CITY" — AND NOT THE INHABITANTS OF ANOTHER CITY. ({SP_(93, 4, "ולא", "יושבי", "עיר", "אחרת")} "and not the inhabitants of another city"): the seducers of their own city — THE INK: the chapter\'s one narrative verb (computed). Fresh.')
srow(93, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"SAYING" — WITH A WARNING. "LET US GO AND SERVE OTHER GODS WHICH YOU HAVE NOT KNOWN." ({SP_(93, 5, "בהתראה")} "with a warning"): the seducers\' speech read as the WARNING the law requires (the English\'s notes: Mishnah Sanhedrin 10:4, Sifrei Numbers 113) — the compile\'s condition. Fresh.')
srow(93, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL INQUIRE AND SEARCH AND ASK DILIGENTLY" (13:15) — SINCE IT IS SAID "AND IT IS TOLD YOU AND YOU HEAR AND INQUIRE DILIGENTLY" (17:4): "DILIGENTLY", "DILIGENTLY" FOR AN ANALOGY — IT TEACHES THAT THEY EXAMINE HIM WITH SEVEN INQUIRIES. ({SP_(93, 6, "היטב", "היטב", "לגזרה", "שוה")} "diligently, diligently, for an analogy"): I2 (checked) on the word\'s two seats — THE SEVEN INQUIRIES (Mishnah Sanhedrin 5:1; the English\'s note counts them from the verse\'s seven words) taught by the chapter for every capital case; 149:1 and 190:7 say it at 17:4 and 19:18. Fresh.')
srow(93, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'THE PROBES — WHENCE? "AND BEHOLD IT IS TRUE, THE THING IS CERTAIN." ({SP_(93, 7, "בדיקות", "מנין")} "the probes — whence"): the verse\'s second clause the second examination. Fresh.')
srow(93, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'IF IN THE END WE INCLUDE PROBES, WHY "INQUIRIES"? INQUIRIES — ONE SAID "I DO NOT KNOW", THEIR TESTIMONY IS VOID; PROBES — ONE SAID "I DO NOT KNOW", EVEN TWO SAID "WE DO NOT KNOW", THEIR TESTIMONY STANDS. ({SP_(93, 8, "עדותם", "בטלה")} "their testimony is void"; {SP_(93, 8, "עדותם", "קימת")} "their testimony stands"): THE TWO EXAMINATIONS\' TWO RULES (Mishnah Sanhedrin 5:2) — a decision table on the witness\'s "I do not know". Fresh.')
srow(93, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'INQUIRIES AND PROBES ALIKE: WHEN THEY CONTRADICT ONE ANOTHER, THEIR TESTIMONY IS VOID. ({SP_(93, 9, "שמכחישים", "זה", "את", "זה")} "that they contradict one another"): the table\'s third row. Fresh.')
srow(93, 10, 'CONTEXT', f'"THIS ABOMINATION WAS DONE IN YOUR MIDST" — TO INCLUDE CONVERTS AND FREED SLAVES. ({SP_(93, 10, "לרבות", "גרים", "ועבדים", "משחררים")} "to include converts and freed slaves"). Fresh.')

srow(94, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"SMITE, YOU SHALL SMITE" (13:16) — WHENCE THAT IF YOU COULD NOT PUT HIM TO DEATH BY THE DEATH SAID FOR HIM, YOU PUT HIM TO DEATH BY ANY OF THE DEATHS SAID, LIGHT OR HEAVY? "SMITE, YOU SHALL SMITE." WHENCE THAT IF HE ESCAPED YOUR HAND HE HAS NOT ESCAPED MINE? "SMITE, YOU SHALL SMITE." The head row of piska 94 ({SP_(94, 1, "המיתו", "באחת", "מכל", "מיתות", "האמורות")} "put him to death by any of the deaths said"): THE INFINITIVE ABSOLUTE read as "by any means" (Tosefta Sanhedrin 12:6) — THE INK: the chapter\'s four (computed). Fresh.')
srow(94, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE INHABITANTS OF THAT CITY" — the verse alone. ({SP_(94, 2, "העיר", "ההיא")} "that city" — THE READ FORM: the shelf quotes the feminine where the DB writes the masculine ketiv, the chapter\'s one written/read pair — computed). Fresh.')
srow(94, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'FROM HERE THEY SAID: THEY DO NOT LET THE CHILDREN LIVE. ABBA HANAN: "FATHERS SHALL NOT BE PUT TO DEATH FOR SONS" (24:16) — OF THE CONDEMNED CITY THE TEXT SPEAKS. "THE INHABITANTS OF THAT CITY" — NOT ANOTHER CITY\'S: FROM HERE THEY SAID, THE DONKEY-DRIVERS AND THE CAMEL-DRIVERS PASSING THROUGH SAVE IT. "WITH THE EDGE OF THE SWORD" — INTO THE SWORD\'S MOUTH, NOT TO DISFIGURE THEM. ({SP_(94, 3, "אין", "מקימים", "את", "הטפלים")} "they do not let the children live"; {SP_(94, 3, "החמרת", "והגמלת")} "the donkey-drivers and the camel-drivers"): THE DISPUTE ON THE CHILDREN (killed / spared by 24:16 — Abba Hanan, Tosefta 14:3\'s R. Akiva) a PARAMETER; the caravan that saves the city (Mishnah Sanhedrin 10:5) a CASE of the count; the sword\'s manner. Fresh.')
srow(94, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"DEVOTE IT" — EXCLUDING THE PROPERTY OF THE RIGHTEOUS OUTSIDE IT. ({SP_(94, 4, "פרט", "לנכסי", "צדיקים", "שבחוצה", "לה")} "excluding the property of the righteous outside it"): THE PROPERTY TABLE begins (94:4-5, 95:1). Fresh.')
srow(94, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND ALL THAT IS IN IT" — TO INCLUDE THE PROPERTY OF THE RIGHTEOUS INSIDE IT. FROM HERE THEY SAID: THE RIGHTEOUS\' PROPERTY INSIDE IS LOST, OUTSIDE IS SAVED; THE WICKED\'S, INSIDE OR OUTSIDE, IS LOST. ({SP_(94, 5, "נכסי", "צדיקים", "שבתוכה", "אובדים")} "the property of the righteous inside it is lost"): Mishnah Sanhedrin 10:5\'s four cells (owner × place) from the verse\'s two clauses. Fresh.')
srow(94, 6, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND ITS CATTLE" — AND NOT CONSECRATED CATTLE. ({SP_(94, 6, "ולא", "בהמת", "הקדש")} "and not consecrated cattle"): the consecrated outside the ban (Tosefta 14:5). Fresh.')

srow(95, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND ALL ITS SPOIL" (13:17) — TO INCLUDE THE PROPERTY OF THE WICKED OUTSIDE IT. The head row of piska 95 ({SP_(95, 1, "לרבות", "נכסי", "רשעים", "שבחוצה", "לה")} "to include the property of the wicked outside it"): the table\'s fourth cell. Fresh.')
srow(95, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'"INTO THE MIDST OF ITS STREET" — IF IT HAS NO STREET, THEY MAKE IT A STREET. ({SP_(95, 2, "אין", "לה", "רחוב", "עושים", "לה", "רחוב")} "if it has no street they make it a street"): "its street" the Torah\'s one seat (computed). Fresh.')
srow(95, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'IF ITS STREET WAS OUTSIDE IT, WHENCE THAT THEY BRING IT INSIDE? "INTO THE MIDST OF ITS STREET." ({SP_(95, 3, "שכונסים", "אותו", "לתוכה")} "that they gather it inside"). Fresh.')
srow(95, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND BURN WITH FIRE THE CITY AND ALL ITS SPOIL" — AND NOT HEAVEN\'S SPOIL: FROM HERE THEY SAID, TREES ATTACHED ARE PERMITTED AND DETACHED FORBIDDEN; CISTERNS, TRENCHES, CAVES AND HOLY WRITINGS PERMITTED, FOR "ITS SPOIL" — NOT HEAVEN\'S. ({SP_(95, 4, "ולא", "שלל", "שמים")} "and not Heaven\'s spoil"): what the fire does not take (Mishnah Sanhedrin 10:6; the English\'s note calls part an interpolation — the row stands whole in both files). Fresh.')
srow(95, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'FROM HERE THEY SAID (MISHNAH SANHEDRIN 10:6): THE CONSECRATED THINGS INSIDE IT ARE REDEEMED, THE HEAVE OFFERINGS ROT, SECOND TITHE AND HOLY WRITINGS ARE HIDDEN. ({SP_(95, 5, "ההקדשות", "שבתוכה", "יפדו")} "the consecrated things inside it are redeemed"): the Mishnah\'s four dispositions cited by the Hebrew row itself — the answer sheet at 11b. Fresh.')
srow(95, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHOLLY TO THE LORD YOUR GOD, AND IT SHALL BE A HEAP FOREVER" — SO IT SAYS: "JOSHUA SWORE AT THAT TIME: CURSED BE THE MAN WHO RISES AND BUILDS THIS CITY, JERICHO" (JOSHUA 6:26); DO WE NOT KNOW ITS NAME IS JERICHO? RATHER — THAT THEY NOT BUILD IT AND CALL IT ANOTHER CITY\'S NAME, NOR BUILD ANOTHER CITY AND CALL IT JERICHO. ({SP_(95, 6, "שלא", "יבנו", "אותה", "ויקראו", "שמה", "עיר", "אחרת")} "that they not build it and call its name another city"): JERICHO THE RUN\'S CASE of the heap (the tape\'s Joshua ahead); the English writes "Josh.6:36" for 6:26 (asserted). Fresh.')
srow(95, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"WITH HIS FIRSTBORN HE SHALL FOUND IT AND WITH HIS YOUNGEST SET UP ITS GATES" (JOSHUA 6:26) — MIGHT IT BE UNWITTING? "ACCORDING TO THE WORD OF THE LORD WHICH HE SPOKE BY JOSHUA SON OF NUN" (1 KINGS 16:34). SAY THEN: HE WAS WILFUL. ({SP_(95, 7, "מזיד", "היה")} "he was wilful"): Hiel\'s rebuilding the curse\'s fulfilment, the intent read from Kings — a run citation beyond the tape. Fresh.')

srow(96, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"IT SHALL NOT BE BUILT AGAIN" (13:17) — YOU SHALL NOT MAKE IT EVEN GARDENS AND ORCHARDS, EVEN A DOVECOTE OF HERODIAN DOVES — R. AKIVA\'S WORDS. The head row of piska 96 ({SP_(96, 1, "אפלו", "גנות", "ופרדסים")} "even gardens and orchards"): "again" read to every use (Mishnah Sanhedrin 10:6). Fresh.')
srow(96, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"NOTHING OF THE DEVOTED THING SHALL CLEAVE TO YOUR HAND" (13:18) — FROM HERE THEY SAID (MISHNAH AVODAH ZARAH 3:9): TOOK A STAFF, A FORK, A SPINDLE OR A ROD — ALL FORBIDDEN FOR BENEFIT; MIXED WITH OTHERS — ALL FORBIDDEN; WHAT DOES HE DO? CARRIES THE BENEFIT TO THE SALT SEA. THE RULE: WHOEVER BENEFITS FROM IDOLATRY CARRIES THE BENEFIT TO THE SALT SEA. ({SP_(96, 2, "יוליך", "הניה", "לים", "המלח")} "he carries the benefit to the Salt Sea"): THE DEVOTED THING\'S BENEFIT — the answer sheet cited by the Hebrew row; Achan\'s "of the devoted thing" (Joshua 7:1) the run\'s case (computed). Fresh.')
srow(96, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"THAT THE LORD MAY TURN FROM THE FIERCENESS OF HIS ANGER" — AS LONG AS IDOLATRY IS IN THE WORLD, FIERCE ANGER IS IN THE WORLD; IDOLATRY REMOVED FROM THE WORLD, FIERCE ANGER REMOVED. ({SP_(96, 3, "כל", "זמן", "שעבודה", "זרה", "בעולם")} "as long as idolatry is in the world"): THE ANGER\'S STATUS KEYED TO IDOLATRY\'S PRESENCE — the compile\'s effect (Achan\'s valley "and the LORD turned from the fierceness of His anger", Joshua 7:26 — computed). Fresh.')
srow(96, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND GIVE YOU MERCY AND HAVE MERCY ON YOU" — TO YOU MERCY, NOT TO OTHERS. FROM HERE RABBAN GAMLIEL SON OF RABBI: AS LONG AS YOU HAVE MERCY ON CREATURES, HEAVEN HAS MERCY ON YOU; NO MERCY ON CREATURES, NO MERCY FROM HEAVEN. "AND MULTIPLY YOU" — AS "I WILL MULTIPLY YOUR SEED AS THE STARS" (GENESIS 26:4). ({SP_(96, 4, "כל", "זמן", "שאתה", "מרחם", "על", "הבריות")} "as long as you have mercy on creatures"): the mercy a two-arm conditional (Tosefta Bava Kamma 9:30); the multiplying Isaac\'s oath. Fresh.')
srow(96, 5, 'CONTEXT', f'"AS HE SWORE TO YOUR FATHERS" — ALL BY THE MERIT OF YOUR FATHERS. ({SP_(96, 5, "הכל", "בזכות", "אבותיך")} "all by the merit of your fathers"): the oath\'s AS_WHEN form (13:18, 19:8 — computed) read as the fathers\' merit (7b\'s parameter). Fresh.')
srow(96, 6, 'CONTEXT', f'"WHEN YOU HEARKEN TO THE VOICE OF THE LORD YOUR GOD" (13:19) — FROM HERE THEY SAID: ONE WHO BEGAN TO HEAR A LITTLE ENDS HEARING MUCH. ({SP_(96, 6, "התחיל", "אדם", "לשמע", "קמעה")} "one who began to hear a little"): 79:1\'s kin. Fresh.')
srow(96, 7, 'CONTEXT', f'"TO KEEP ALL HIS COMMANDMENTS WHICH I COMMAND YOU TODAY" — THAT A LIGHT COMMANDMENT BE AS DEAR AS A WEIGHTY ONE. ({SP_(96, 7, "שתהא", "מצוה", "קלה", "חביבה")} "that a light commandment be dear"): 82:1\'s reading at the footer — the chapter framed by one sentence. Fresh.')
srow(96, 8, 'CONTEXT', f'"TO DO THE RIGHT IN THE EYES OF THE LORD YOUR GOD" — THIS IS WHAT R. ISHMAEL SAYS: "THE RIGHT" — IN THE EYES OF HEAVEN. ({SP_(96, 8, "בעיני", "שמים")} "in the eyes of Heaven"): 79:2\'s pair (the good in Heaven\'s eyes, the right in men\'s) closed here with "the right" Heaven\'s. THE LAST ROW OF THE CHAPTER — 96:9-12 open with 14:1 and wait for chapter 14\'s sitting. Fresh.')

assert sorted(S) == [(93, r) for r in range(1, 11)] + [(94, r) for r in range(1, 7)] + [(95, r) for r in range(1, 8)] + [(96, r) for r in range(1, 9)], sorted(S)
